# Infrastructure layer

Implements the ports defined in `application/`. Never contains business rules
— only translates between Prisma and the application layer.

- **Repositories** (`persistence/prisma/prisma-<feature>.repository.ts`)
  implement the matching port interface exactly; one class per aggregate.
- **Mappers** (`persistence/prisma/mappers/*.mapper.ts`) convert Prisma models
  to application read models — keep Prisma types out of the application layer.
- Wrap Prisma errors via `prisma-error.ts` helpers before rethrowing, so
  Presentation never sees raw Prisma error codes.
- **Auth**: `jose` for JWT (`jose-auth-token.service.ts`), `bcrypt` for
  password hashing (`bcrypt-password-hasher.ts`) — both implement application
  ports (`auth-token.service.ts`, `password-hasher.ts`).
- **Config** (`config/env.ts`): all `process.env` reads go through
  `loadEnv()` — never scatter raw `process.env` access across the codebase.
- **Logging**: use the injected logger (`logging/logger.ts`), not
  `console.log`, so output stays structured for stdout/stderr aggregation.
